{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I. In the silence.</b> Some say it is from the root דם, like לחלוחית, but the correct interpretation is like כריתות, like נדמה מלך ישראל (Hosea 10:15)." "<b>Sheol.</b> It is the grave that is at the bottom of the earth, the opposite of the heavens which are above forever. The proof is ואציעה שאול הנך (Psalms 139:8). It is not Gehinnom at all." "<b>I am counted.</b> From the root לא נפקד ממנו איש (Numbers 31:49), and it is a rare form, likewise in the language of Kedar. Some say פקדתי means 'a remnant has departed from me,' like בני יצאוני (Jeremiah 10:20), and others say פקדתי means 'he has counted more.'" "And the meaning of <b>the remainder of my years</b> is like את מספר ימיך אמלא (Exodus 23:26), and there I explained it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:53.593294430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}